 *   **Watertightness:** The method relies on the Jordan curve theorem. Models with cracks, inner walls separating volumes, or nested shells (where the inner shell is considered empty) are not watertight under this definition and produce incorrect interiors [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Clipping:** Polygons must not be clipped by the near and far planes of the camera. Use Depth Clamp (e.g., NV_depth_clamp extension) to clamp depth values to the frustum, ensuring all intersections are counted [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Voxel Shift:** The voxel grid is shifted by half a voxel along the Z-axis because the bitmask is based on the voxel the fragment falls into. This can be counteracted by adding half a voxel to the fragment's distance in the shader [S1, unofficial].
-*   **API Limitations:** DirectX does not support bitwise blending operations needed for correct accumulation. For DX9, texture tiling is required [S1, unofficial].
